## Portions derived from upstream

Volt.py is a rewrite of https://github.com/ThetaInterface/volt, which was
published **without a license file**. Under copyright law that means the
upstream author reserved all rights to it and granted no permission to
redistribute it, so the MIT terms above cover only the parts written for this
rewrite.

Specifically, the following came from upstream and stay under their original
owner's rights:

* `volt/prompts.py` — the prompt texts, copied from the upstream
  `bin/data.dart` without changes to their wording;
* the world data schema and its identifiers (`actor_player`, `loc_*`,
  `stateChanges` types, the `Time`/`Actor`/`Location` field names).

To relicense those parts under MIT as well, permission from the upstream author
is required — until then, do not present this project as MIT-licensed in full.